From 9923ca360efef89d39af5eac0f08cfe5a148dff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shapey Review <review@shapey.local>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:29:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] refactor(worker): split the 1190-line src/index.js into
 focused modules

index.js mixed the public HTTP router, shared helpers, the Room
Durable Object (lifecycle, directory bridge, seats, chat, polls,
message dispatch and the AI demo bot) in one file.

- lib.js          exported helpers: CORS, json, seat tokens, chat
                  cleaning, poll snapshots, shared constants
- router.js       the public fetch handler (/health, /api/rooms,
                  /ws/{code}); re-exports Room for the DO binding
- room.js         the Room Durable Object core: room fetch routes
                  (create/info/directory/rate-limit/ws upgrade),
                  alarm, broadcasts, directory publishing
- room-seats.js   seat claiming, spectator joins, chat
- room-polls.js   audience poll lifecycle
- room-messages.js the WebSocket message dispatcher
- room-demo.js    the AI-vs-AI demo bot
- index.js        entry: re-exports router + Room (wrangler main)

The Room behaviour modules are prototype mixins composed onto the
class, so every method keeps the same this. Verified with the unit
tests (36 pass), wrangler deploy --dry-run bundling, wrangler dev
integration-smoke (origin guard, PvP scoring/reconnect, polls, chat,
Tag, demo auto-play) and the two-browser PvP browser-smoke.
